"Tracks changes in ordered rank over time while deliberately discarding absolute numeric gaps.\n\nUse when: Relative position is the question and entities are ranked repeatedly. Only a manageable number of trajectories need individual tracking.\n\nAvoid when: Readers need the size of score differences rather than ordering alone.\n\nVisual grammar: Horizontal position encodes successive ranking occasions. Vertical position encodes ordinal rank, with rank one consistently at the top.\n\nBuild: Rank entities independently at every occasion using an explicit tie rule. Connect each entity’s ranks in temporal order. Label paths at clear endpoints and display rank ticks as integers.\n\nCheck: Check the ranking direction and tie method are stated. Verify missing entities are not assigned artificial bottom ranks. Confirm equal rank spacing does not imply equal score differences.\n\nPitfalls: Crossings encode rank reversals and are intrinsic; use a rank heatmap by default when many crossings obscure tracking. Smooth curves must not suggest valid fractional ranks between occasions.\n\nExample: Track synthetic team standings across eight rounds and label the top five trajectories at the final round.\n\nAlternatives: Slope chart, Lasagna plot, Line chart."
